Bug 2063939 - Fix signature not inserted below in plaintext forward.

  The forward container div needs to be filled with something, otherwise the editor removes it.

  We didn't check the AI analysis:

  Root cause confirmed in M-C: DeleteNode() lands in EditorBase::DeleteNodeWithTransaction(),
  which refuses to remove any node failing HTMLEditUtils::IsRemovableNode() and returns NS_ERROR_EDITOR_UNEXPECTED_DOM_TREE:

    // Do nothing if the node is read-only.
    if (IsHTMLEditor() && NS_WARN_IF(!HTMLEditUtils::IsRemovableNode(aContent))) {
      return NS_ERROR_EDITOR_UNEXPECTED_DOM_TREE;
    }

  IsRemovableNode() only allows deleting nodes whose parent carries the NODE_IS_EDITABLE flag (or padding <br>s).
  The synthetic moz-forward-container div you insert programmatically apparently no longer gets that flag in the
  plaintext mail composer — that's why the sibling-<br> deletion (parent = editable body) still works,
  while extraBr (parent = the div) fails.

diff --git a/mailnews/compose/src/nsMsgCompose.cpp b/mailnews/compose/src/nsMsgCompose.cpp
--- a/mailnews/compose/src/nsMsgCompose.cpp
+++ b/mailnews/compose/src/nsMsgCompose.cpp
@@ -713,11 +713,22 @@ nsMsgCompose::ConvertAndLoadComposeWindo
               }
             }
           }
 
-          // Clean up the <br> we inserted.
-          rv = htmlEditor->DeleteNode(extraBr, false, 1);
-          NS_ENSURE_SUCCESS(rv, rv);
+          // The placeholder <br> is gone by now: While inserting the text,
+          // the editor removes a <br> following the insertion point as an
+          // "unnecessary line break" and may create its own padding <br> for
+          // the trailing empty line, either directly in the div or in the
+          // last quotation span. Remove whatever trailing <br> is actually
+          // there to avoid an extra empty line after the forwarded content.
+          nsCOMPtr<nsIContent> lastChild = divElem->GetLastChild();
+          if (lastChild && !lastChild->IsHTMLElement(nsGkAtoms::br) &&
+              lastChild->IsElement()) {
+            lastChild = lastChild->GetLastChild();
+          }
+          if (lastChild && lastChild->IsHTMLElement(nsGkAtoms::br)) {
+            lastChild->Remove();
+          }
         }
 
         // Use our own function instead of nsEditor::EndOfDocument() because
         // we don't want to position at the end of the div we've just created.
